# The 5.1 GB OpenStax source. NEVER commit this path: it is untracked bulk data, and a
# symlink committed here was checked out over the real directory in the main worktree and
# destroyed it. Keep it ignored so `git add -A` cannot pick it up.
corpus/raw
build/model_*.bin
overnight.log
probe_*.txt
d2_*.txt

# figure-generation environment (tools/paper/requirements.txt)
.venv-fig/

# paper build outputs (regenerable; tools/paper/check_paper.py removes LaTeX's working files after
# each build). paper/paper.pdf and paper/paper-arxiv.pdf ARE tracked: the folder is the deliverable.
paper/*.aux
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/paper-arxiv.tex
# the arXiv upload, rebuilt from paper/ by check_paper.py --preprint
submission/arxiv-source.zip
# original photographs and video of the calculator (large; see submission/PHOTOS.md)
media/
# the re-encoded videos and the TMLR supplementary ZIP, rebuilt by tools/paper/make_media.py --video
submission/supplementary/*.mp4
submission/supplementary.zip

# int8 exports for host scoring on the device decoder (regenerable)
build/int8/

# ---- 2026-09-26 tidy-up ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build/ holds what `make` produces. The few DATA files there stay tracked (model4096*.bin,
# tok4096.tok, tok_reference.json, transfer/README.txt): an ignore rule never untracks a tracked
# file, and a new data file needs `git add -f`.
build/*
# host tools compiled by `make` next to their sources
tools/eval/evalcli
tools/eval/provcli
tools/eval/shapecli
tools/eval/test_eval
# local leftovers, kept rather than deleted (attic/README.txt)
attic/
# model checkpoints are too large for git; train/README.md lists the ones that matter and must be
# backed up. Checkpoints tracked before this rule stay tracked.
train/*.pt
train/archive_*/
